# Temporary execution-copy Sync measurement

This future-only standalone Windows Go program measures the specific copy
operation used by the API namespace auxiliary. It uses only the Go standard
library and does not import the Hub, start children, execute either copied
test image, invoke a shell, use the network, or read Source/Go-cache payloads.

## Fixed roles

- Input: `@@RECOVERY_APPROVED_WORK_AREA@@\r7\x149e4a76727c\incoming-original.exe`.
- Exact input SHA256: `d237704913484fe2931860793badbfdaadb3bb216f5c436b8d01bdf2301d3e60`.
- Input authority: the root's original API v3 receiving; this program issues no authority.
- Output: the new, absent directory `@@RECOVERY_APPROVED_WORK_AREA@@\mcp-acceptance-rebuild-20261127-v1\namespace-copy-probe-v1-data`.
- Its only files: `with-sync.exe`, `without-sync.exe`, `probe-receipt.json`.

The two EXE files are DATA copies, never launched. Existing output is refused;
there are no overwrite, delete, trash, retry or cleanup operations. Ancestors
and leaf kinds are checked for ordinary non-reparse paths. Source bytes, size,
mtime and file identity are checked before/after; both complete copied hashes
and both reopened destination hashes must equal the exact input SHA.

## Root-owned preparation and execution

Build this single file with the already-pinned Go compiler under the existing
original native owner, using an independently copied closed cache if needed:

```text
<go.exe> build -o <new-stage-output>\namespace-copy-probe.exe <this-directory>\main_windows.go
<new-stage-output>\namespace-copy-probe.exe
```

The program accepts no operands. Its author has not compiled or run it.
The root reviews the source, freezes its pins, builds, and runs it in the
separately authorized native stage. No active full59f cache is an input.

## Measured operations

All duration fields are integer nanoseconds from Go monotonic `time.Now`/`time.Since`.
Divide by 1,000,000 to obtain milliseconds.

| Field | Included work |
| --- | --- |
| `copy_ns` | The original `io.Copy(io.MultiWriter(target, sha256), source)` operation. |
| `sync_ns` | One destination `File.Sync()` only in the with-sync case. `sync_called` distinguishes omission from a completed zero-duration measurement. |
| `destination_close_ns` | The original destination's single `Close` call. |
| `source_close_ns` | The original source reader's single `Close` call. |
| `readback_ns` | Ordinary-path checks plus reopening, full destination hashing, and checked close. |
| `total_ns` | All work in one copy sample, including opens, checks and the listed operations. |

Copy or Sync failure still leads to checked closes of both opened files.
Close errors are preserved and prevent DATA success. Final receipt writing and
its durability Sync occur after these measurements. A root must also require
the original probe exit0 and normal native/IO closure before accepting the report.

## Interpretation

The input hash check happens before both samples and warms its file data.
There is one observation per mode, in fixed order: with-sync then without-sync.
The outputs have different fresh names. Cache, antivirus, storage load and order
can affect times; this is not a statistical benchmark or a full replication of
the namespace preparation path. The measured Sync duration is the useful direct
quantity; a difference between whole-sample durations alone does not prove causality.

The namespace helper and all admission/Go-test/native-owner predicates remain
unchanged. This probe cannot grant API test PASS, namespace admission qualification,
full-run closure, CLI closure, cache handoff, or a deadline increase. If measured
cost is insufficient to explain the refusal, the next candidate is narrow timing
instrumentation of the original admission path, not an arbitrary larger budget.
